 "envelope_text": {
  "thruster_axis_alignment": {"status": "PROPOSED", "statement": "The thrust axis is parallel to the flight (anti-ram) direction, collinear with the drag axis of the intake, and passes through the spacecraft centre of mass; the lateral offset and angular tolerances are TBD - require the spacecraft AOCS disturbance-torque budget (owner / spacecraft). The flight mount carries a measurable alignment reference (datum surfaces or an optical reference) so the as-installed thrust axis can be surveyed.", "flight_status": "FLIGHT-REPRESENTATIVE"},
  "cg_estimate": {"status": "NOT_COMPUTABLE", "statement": "No row has a layout position yet (no preliminary geometry from H2-1..H2-6 and no spacecraft configuration). The builder computes CG = sum(m_i r_i)/sum(m_i) once every mass-bearing row carries a position; the Xe consumption term (5.4 kg fixed cathode term) moves the CG by m_Xe x (r_tank - r_CG)/M over the mission. PROPOSED layout rule: Xe tank centroid on or near the thrust axis and near the spacecraft CG, so Xe depletion does not create a growing thrust-axis offset.", "flight_status": "FLIGHT-REPRESENTATIVE"},
  "spacecraft_mounting_interface": {"status": "PROPOSED", "items": [
   "M-01 propulsion-module mounting plane to the spacecraft structure: bolt pattern, fastener size and preload TBD (spacecraft)",
   "M-02 thruster mount with alignment reference and adjustable shimming; thruster floats electrically (HW-ELEC-01), so the mount includes the electrical isolation of the thruster body; bonding scheme TBD (H2-4)",
   "M-03 conductive / radiative thermal interface of the thruster mount and the PPU baseplate: controlled path, values PENDING H2-5",
   "M-04 intake mounted at the ram face with the compressor directly behind the intake throat (compressor inlet area constraint in the derived envelope)",
   "M-05 Xe tank mount near the spacecraft CG (see cg_estimate)",
   "M-06 harness connectors at the PPU; separation of discharge return from RF / microwave return if a pre-ionizer module is fitted (HW-ELEC-03)"
  ], "flight_status": "FLIGHT-REPRESENTATIVE"},
  "intake_to_thruster_layout": {"status": "PROPOSED", "constraints": [
   "L-01 series order along the flight axis: intake (ram face) -> protective/filter stage -> compressor -> buffer/plenum -> atmospheric metering valve -> [reserved RF pre-ionization module interface, IP-UP ... IP-DN] -> HALL_INLET_Z0 -> Hall exit plane (aft)",
   "L-02 the reserved pre-ionizer volume between the plenum/valve and the Hall inlet is kept free in the baseline so that fitting RF after H-1 does not require redesigning the thruster (A5 reserved_interface); its envelope is PENDING docs/interfaces/preionizer_module/",
   "L-03 the plenum-to-anode gas path length and cross-section set the conductance at 0.05-1 Pa; kept as short as the layout allows; numeric conductance PENDING docs/hardware/h2/h2_3_gas_path_plenum/",
   "L-04 Xe branch separate from the atmospheric path: tank -> regulator -> metering -> (a) cathode line and (b) ignition/transition line to the anode side; the cathode gas never crosses HALL_INLET_Z0 (HW-C1-04)",
   "L-05 the cathode is placed and shielded to limit exposure to the atmospheric plume (A5 risk 3; H2-2)",
   "L-06 plume keep-out: no intake, radiator or solar-array surface inside the thruster plume keep-out cone; half-angle TBD - requires plume divergence data of the Vyovrinda thruster on the delivered feed (the PPS1350 datasheet's 40 deg 'reduced beam divergence' is a xenon analog statement, context only)",
   "L-07 the compressor inlet spans a large fraction of the intake frontal area (derived envelope: A_inlet_min / A_intake), so the compressor sits in the intake cross-section, not in a narrow duct"
  ], "flight_status": "FLIGHT-REPRESENTATIVE"}
 },
